## Summary

I've built a complete Anserini Prebuilt Index Evaluator web application that satisfies all PRD requirements.

### What was built

**Backend** (`app/server.py`, ~800 lines): A Flask server that drives everything through the Anserini fatjar CLI:
- `io.anserini.cli.PrebuiltIndexRegistry --type inverted --list` → catalog (109 indexes)
- `io.anserini.cli.TopicsRegistry --list` → topics (1493 topics)
- Reproduction YAMLs from `reproduce/from-prebuilt-indexes/configs/*.yaml` → 274 evaluable pairings across 45 indexes
- `io.anserini.search.SearchCollection` → generates real TREC run files
- `io.anserini.eval.TrecEval` → evaluates against real qrels

**Frontend** (`app/templates/index.html`, `app/static/app.js`, `app/static/app.css`):
- Searchable/filterable catalog with Evaluable/Catalog-Only badges
- Evaluation panel that auto-shows the paired topics + qrels + metric options
- Metric selector with `nDCG@10`, `Recall@1000` always available (per PRD)
- Result card with score, run metadata, run/eval file paths, and previews
- All labels translated to exact `trec_eval` arg strings (e.g. `nDCG@10` → `-c -m ndcg_cut.10`)

**Unit tests** (`app/test_server.py`): 13 tests covering metric translation and pairing logic.

**E2E test** (`e2e/test_app.py` + `e2e/run_e2e.sh`): Playwright browser test that:
- Opens the app, verifies the registry-derived catalog has 109+ entries and at least one catalog-only entry
- Selects CACM (the default), confirms qrels pairing is shown
- Selects nDCG@10 (with Recall@1000 fallback), clicks Run Evaluation
- Verifies a real numeric score (0.4543 — matches the smoke-test expected value)
- Verifies run/eval artifact paths exist on disk, contain TREC-formatted results, and have >1000 lines
- Anti-mock checks: the score must be in [0.4, 0.5] for CACM nDCG@10

### Test results

```
=== Unit tests ===
All 13 tests passed

=== E2E test ===
e2e test PASSED
  catalog items: 109 (real registry, not mocked)
  catalog-only: 80
  score: 0.4543 (real Anserini nDCG@10 on CACM)
```

